{"diagnosis": "Fetch progress signal max_addr stuck at 0x00000000 instead of walking the 256-word NOP memory, causing TRAP no-progress and tohost FAIL 0xdead. Expected reg_next_pc/mem_addr to advance by instruction width each fetch. Root cause in excerpt lines 1526-1527 where reg_next_pc <= current_pc discards the increment so current_pc never advances.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picorv32.v b/picorv32.v
--- a/picorv32.v
+++ b/picorv32.v
@@ -1526,2 +1526,2 @@
 				reg_pc <= current_pc;
-				reg_next_pc <= current_pc;
+				reg_next_pc <= current_pc + (compressed_instr ? 2 : 4);
", "expected": "tohost PASS, max_addr=0x000003fc advancing, no no-progress TRAP"}

